<https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso27001/iso27001> dcterms:license "Apache-2.0" ;
	dcterms:source "https://www.iso.org/standard/82875.html"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	dcterms:title "ISO/IEC 27001:2022 information security management system records" ;
	pav:version "2022/Amd 1:2024" ;
	a linkml:SchemaDefinition ;
	rdfs:seeAlso "https://lmodel.github.io/iso27001"^^xsd:anyURI , "https://www.iso.org/standard/82875.html"^^xsd:anyURI , "https://www.iso.org/standard/88435.html"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:note "Every record that other records refer to has an isms_id, and a reference holds that identifier. IsmsManagementSystem holds each kind of record in a list of its own." , "ISO/IEC 27001 is copyright ISO and IEC, and none of its text is reproduced here. Each element cites the clause or Annex A control it models by number, in the iso27001_clause or annex_a_control annotation, and its description is this project's own words. A licence holder can merge the standard's wording into a private copy with the overlay that src/iso27001/schema/OVERLAY.md describes." , "The mappings name terms of the released lmodel/oscal, lmodel/spdx and lmodel/nist-sp-800-53 schemas, and come from the SSSOM files in src/iso27001/mappings/." , "The terms follow ISO/IEC 27000, which ISO/IEC 27001 refers to for them; the edition current on the pinned date is ISO/IEC 27000:2026." , "The version is the edition the schema models, 2022, with its one amendment, Amd 1:2024, and source is ISO's page for that edition. ISO Open Data's records of both, and of ISO/IEC 27002:2022 and ISO/IEC 27000:2026, are copied to src/iso27001/schema/iso-open-data/ as of the date in the annotations, and scripts/check_upstream_release.py reports when ISO publishes another supplement or edition. The release tags are the schema's own versions." ;
